#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:40
#: 17d95e969fe44e6aad56fd09f9792074
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:41
#: 18c11426371046ac87a281bb99e997f7
msgid "The default RC input is configured on USART1. RC could  be applied instead to a different UART port such as  and set the protocol to receive RC data ``SERIALn_PROTOCOL`` = 23 and change :ref:`SERIAL1 _PROTOCOL <SERIAL1_PROTOCOL>` to something other than '23'. For RC protocols other than unidirectional, the USART1_TX pin will need to be used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:43
#: 84a4373431124f30a2363a6cd0af4249
msgid "FPort would require :ref:`SERIAL1_OPTIONS<SERIAL1_OPTIONS>` be set to \"15\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:44
#: fcc60414a53f4364bfad450f97af47d0
msgid "CRSF would require :ref:`SERIAL1_OPTIONS<SERIAL1_OPTIONS>` be set to \"0\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:45
#: 4bea2b7d9388485587f399e85bf6da0a
msgid "SRXL2 would require :ref:`SERIAL1_OPTIONS<SERIAL1_OPTIONS>` be set to \"4\" and connects only the TX pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:46
#: 775b0a43c9084b37b619fcafed2d1c58
msgid "PPM is not supported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:49
#: 2912f55e0f2745b49341f1022e6513c3
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:50
#: 1e88b78699224b99908419f314a72504
msgid "The SequreH743 supports OSD using its MAX7456by default, and simultaneously DisplayPort using UART7 on the HD VTX connector if :ref:`OSD_TYPE2<OSD_TYPE2>` is set to \"5\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:53
#: 7063953740204b48a1c720058f437da1
msgid "VTX Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:54
#: 0d0dcf4660714eed972d878dd19219fe
msgid "The SH1.0-6P connector supports a DJI Air Unit / HD VTX connection. Protocol defaults to DisplayPort. Pin 1 of the connector is 9v so be careful not to connect this to a peripheral that can not tolerate this voltage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:57
#: 5fb15de7a0474d8d8d2307ba8879e1ad
msgid "Camera control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:58
#: 4ea412f27e30419d9d084326d1ff0a6a
msgid "GPIO 81 is a pin for PWM camera control (CC pad) which is not supported by ArduPilot. It can be used as a general GPIO pin. By default RELAY2 is configured to control this pin and sets the GPIO high."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:61
#: d4d29b65043147e8ab87f2246cf5e078
msgid "PWM Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:62
#: 57ac0ef1fbab4648b7331b8e2bdd99df
msgid "The SequreH743 supports up to 9 PWM or DShot outputs. The pads for motor output M1 to M9 are provided on both the motor connectors and on separate pads, plus separate pad for LED strip (default configuration) or another PWM output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:66
#: 94de4566ac2f4af080bf17ff4618243a
msgid "The PWM is in 4 groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:69
#: 7b911e6828054015a5a5dca69b2a487f
msgid "PWM 1-4   in group1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:70
#: 094274a1072844868af3f61ce850551f
msgid "PWM 5-6   in group2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:71
#: 949e8c5a074c42b781f2ef1d431cb26c
msgid "PWM 7-8   in group3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:72
#: d577becde4844a758b7ae5dbe9ac8543
msgid "PWM 9 (LED)   in group4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:74
#: eb10c40958c242ddb1827971629a93f2
msgid "Channels within the same group need to use the same output rate. If any channel in a group uses DShot then all channels in the group need to use DShot. Channels 1-8 support bi-directional dshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:79
#: 92c6dafbe9124896ba62acb964ec92fb
msgid "Battery Monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:80
#: 56ef26fa2e2440fe8ace303326d8b35a
msgid "The board has a internal voltage sensor and connections on the ESC connector for an external current sensor input. The voltage sensor can handle up to 6S LiPo batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:82
#: 8a3c95fcdd1c4ffdb66ecd3f7427688e
msgid "The default battery parameters are: * :ref:`BATT_MONITOR<BATT_MONITOR>` = 4 * :ref:`BATT_VOLT_PIN<BATT_VOLT_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 13 * :ref:`BATT_CURR_PIN<BATT_CURR_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 12 (CURR pin) * :ref:`BATT_VOLT_MULT<BATT_VOLT_MULT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 11.0 * :ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 17.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:90
#: 5c0a4bffa3e54a9e938a838991c3c14e
msgid "Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:91
#: d8fa67284ab9488687f55445ef072bee
msgid "The SequreH743 does not have a built-in compass, but you can attach an external compass using I2C on the SDA and SCL pads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:94
#: 92e4ffea48b34b0cb7e0b68f835ac4e8
msgid "Loading Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:95
#: 59b0b9ad156449d6888ee0ad4227842f
msgid "Firmware for these boards can be found `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__ in sub-folders labeled \"SequreH743\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:97
#: 5233889f54ac45f39f7f64cfadb29227
msgid "Initial firmware load can be done with DFU by plugging in USB with the bootloader button pressed. Then you should load the \"with_bl.hex\" firmware, using your favourite DFU loading tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-sequreh743.rst:101
#: 0b1507bd6f304567a41ab5156a766fb2
msgid "Once the initial firmware is loaded you can update the firmware using any ArduPilot ground station software. Updates should be done with the \\*.apj firmware files."
msgstr ""
